final result: combined config converges at 2.505 bpc over 15 epochs

15-epoch run of the combined architecture (N=4096 + pointer-chain pool +
multi-epoch + decay=1e-4) converged at 2.505 bits/char, with diminishing
returns visible by epoch 10.

Convergence trajectory:
  epoch 1:  2.847 bpc (54.5% argmax accuracy)
  epoch 3:  2.596 bpc (58.9%)
  epoch 5:  2.544 bpc (59.6%)
  epoch 7:  2.524 bpc (59.7%)
  epoch 10: 2.512 bpc (60.1%)
  epoch 12: 2.508 bpc (60.0%)
  epoch 15: 2.505 bpc (60.3%)

Gap to tiny transformer ceiling (2.39): 0.115 bits, down from 0.45 at the
start of the session. ~75% of the gap closed by stacking three architectural
improvements (substrate width, pointer-chain memory, multi-epoch with
decay) that compound rather than just adding.

Argmax accuracy improvement: 54.6% (baseline) -> 60.3% (final), confirming
the signal-profile diagnosis was actionable and the multi-epoch+pool
combination directly attacked the Stage B bottleneck.

Updates handoff doc with final convergence curve.

